#!/usr/bin/env python
"""
You need access to getsentry/getsentry to use this script. It's not trivial. You need access to
the sentry-ecosystems organization. Create your GitHub application using that organization. Details
are listed in the docs link below.

READ: https://develop.sentry.dev/integrations/github/

Run a getsentry server with `devservices serve --ngrok=yourname.ngrok.io`. Register a new GitHub
installation. Add your test repository (created under the sentry-ecosystems GitHub organization).
Update the metadata in the RPC client below to match yours.

You only need ngrok to run the installation step. As long as you don't drop your database you can
re-use its state without ngrok.
"""

